{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 feels like a useful addition to my Fire TV and connected home setup because it adds a larger display, which gives me a clearer reason to choose it than another voice-only speaker.",
    "The portable hard drive fits a practical need suggested by my recent camcorder purchase: backing up recorded videos. Video storage and connection accessories feel relevant when they support equipment I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV Stick feels redundant because I already have a Fire TV Stick 4K and a Fire TV television. Sharing the same ecosystem does not give me a reason to buy another device with overlapping functions.",
    "The Echo Dots do not address a clear need for another speaker, and the internal SSD assumes a computer upgrade I am not planning. The USB-C cables also lack a connection to a charging need established by my recent purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My use of Alexa and Fire TV seems to have been taken as interest in more Alexa devices, even when they repeat functions I already have.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in storage and cables, although portable video backup, internal computer storage, and phone charging serve different needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters now is whether an item adds a useful capability or supports a recent purchase. The larger smart display and portable backup drive give me clearer reasons to act than another streaming device or speaker.",
    "Accessory relevance depends on an actual need and compatibility. I would check whether I need another HDMI cable and whether the microSD card and its capacity work with my camcorder before choosing them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my connected home and video interests, but sometimes confused useful additions with redundant devices or accessories whose need is still unproven."
}"}
